From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:52:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: on iPhone the catalog patch says it belongs in the
 built binary

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A runtime write into main's code is not possible on iPhone: the app's pages are signed, so the kernel accepts the
 write and kills the process with CODESIGNING / Invalid Page the moment the game executes that page again (seen in
 an .ips at main+0xad1ae0, the same page the patch had touched). The engine's own writable alias is built only off
 iPhone for exactly this reason. On iPhone the applier now says the patch belongs in the built binary instead of
 writing, so the run is unchanged and nothing crashes.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/host/hle_npln.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_npln.c b/dm/host/hle_npln.c
index d40cd42..8682339 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_npln.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_npln.c
@@ -206,6 +206,14 @@ int dm_npln_apply(uint64_t title_id) {
                 row->build, (unsigned long long)row->offset);
             continue;
         }
+#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+        // On iPhone the app's pages are signed: a write is accepted and then the process is killed the moment the
+        // game executes that page again (CODESIGNING / "Invalid Page"). The engine's own writable alias is built
+        // only off iPhone for the same reason. The catalog patch therefore belongs in the binary before signing.
+        LOG("[npln] patch for %s at 0x%llx belongs in the built binary: on iPhone the code pages are signed",
+            row->build, (unsigned long long)row->offset);
+        continue;
+#else
         if (!dm_page_writable(at, row->patched_len)) {
             LOG("[npln] patch for %s at 0x%llx: the image refuses to be written, left alone",
                 row->build, (unsigned long long)row->offset);
@@ -214,6 +222,7 @@ int dm_npln_apply(uint64_t title_id) {
         memcpy(at, row->patched, row->patched_len);
         dm_page_code_again(at, row->patched_len);
         written++;
+#endif
         LOG("[npln] patched %s at 0x%llx (%zu bytes)", row->build, (unsigned long long)row->offset, row->patched_len);
     }
     if (!known_build && g_nrows)
